  "Each case's graph is in worldGraph's shape with only the keys the reader reads.",
  "A case's want holds the keys it tests; a case marked whole holds the entire answer, keys in order.",
  "Every want was worked by hand from the page's rules.",
  "A graph is what worldGraph serves the visitor, so a link to an element they may not see is no edge here (the graph never holds an edge to a non-node): the place-not-seen case is a Character with no location edge.",
  "Why hops defaults to 1 (measured 2026-11-01 on four public graphs, five heads): with no reach limit the top head takes most of a world (7,347 of Sikelia's 8,899 nodes, 84 of Blood Meridian's 101, 89 of Moppetopia's 163); at one hop the clusters are Moppetopia 28, 11, 7, 5, 3 and Sikelia 57, 29, 27, 25, 17."
